  "query_preview": "..\n(This evening through next Friday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Skies are mostly sunny across northern\nand central Nevada this afternoon. Highs are generally in the 30s\nwith only a few locations seeing the 40s. Winds are light. Clouds\ncan be seen streaming across California at this time. The clouds\nare expected to arrive later this evening and through the\novernight, which will help to limit how cold we get. Overnight low\ntemperatures will be in the teens and 20s with light winds. \n\nAll models are showing the upcoming storm system to be weaker and\ndrier than previous runs. This feature will be moving through the\nforecast area Sunday and Monday morning with light snow showers or\nflurries. Not much in the way of accumulation is expected. Highs\ntomorrow will continue to remain in the 30s and 40s with light\nwinds. Overnight lows will drop into the teens and 20s. If enough\nsnow remains on the ground and melts during Sunday, there is a low\nprobability that patchy freezing fog could develop from the more\nmoist airmass early Monday morning across the valleys in northern\nNevada.\n\nUpper ridging continues to be progged to build into the area\nMonday with the ridge axis maximizing late Monday afternoon and\nevening before shifting to the east. Highs Monday will remain in\nthe 30s and 40s. Winds are expected to remain light under the\nridge. Look for quiet and dry weather Monday night with lows in\nthe teens and 20s.\n\nFrom Tuesday to Wednesday, models are shown diverging on the next\nsystem for the mid-week portion. Newer runs are depicting a weaker\ntrough with a little less moisture. Snow and precipitation amounts\nhave come down quite a bit during this timeframe and temperatures\nare a bit on the warmer side. High temperatures will be in the \n30s to low 40s Tuesday with rising temperatures into the 40s by \nWednesday. Overnight lows will be in the 20s and 30s. Winds are \nlooking fairly light through the period.\n\nOn Thanksgiving and Friday, even warmer temperatures are expected\nwith readings in the low to upper 40s with generally light winds.\nThere is not too much in the way of precipitation expected. Lows \nwill be in the 20s and 30s.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence exists in the \ngeneral warming trend through the mid week portions. However, low\nconfidence remains in precipitation type, timing, and coverage \nfor Sunday into Monday. Very low confidence for the mid-week\nsystem as models have backed way off on this feature.",
